nio: do not stall on IOBSD before finding the root

The photograph of run 592 stops inside setconf(), before the
ROOT-mount mark that was added just after it.  setconf() calls
IOFindBSDRoot(), whose first act is to wait for a service in
kIOServiceMatchedState carrying IOBSD, with a 30-second bound.

There is no such service.  publishResource("IOBSD") sets a property
on gIOResources; it does not create a matched service, so
copyExistingServices() finds nothing and waitForMatchingService()
sleeps until its deadline.  That deadline is a tick timeout and the
clock is not ticking this early in the boot, so the wait never
returns and bsd_init stops here.

The root filesystem on this board is the mockfs image in RAM; no
matched filesystem driver is needed to mount it.  Remove the stall.
The later root-matching wait is guarded by "if (matching)" and the
rd=md0 memory-device path takes its own exit before it, so no later
code depends on the values this block used to set.

diff --git a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
index 4055934..2c1b0b1 100644
--- a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
@@ -741,18 +741,15 @@ IOFindBSDRoot( char * rootName, unsigned int rootNameSize,
 
 	int xchar, dchar;
 
-	// stall here for anyone matching on the IOBSD resource to finish (filesystems)
-	matching = IOService::serviceMatching(gIOResourcesKey);
-	assert(matching);
-	matching->setObject(gIOResourceMatchedKey, gIOBSDKey);
-
-	if ((service = IOService::waitForMatchingService(matching, 30ULL * kSecondScale))) {
-		OSSafeReleaseNULL(service);
-	} else {
-		IOLog("!BSD\n");
-	}
-	matching->release();
-	matching = NULL;
+	/* nio: the root filesystem here is the mockfs RAMDisk, not a volume
+	 * published by a matched filesystem driver.  The wait below asks for
+	 * a service in kIOServiceMatchedState with IOBSD; publishResource() sets
+	 * a property on gIOResources but never makes such a service, so there
+	 * is nothing to find.  Its 30-second bound is a tick deadline and the
+	 * clock is not ticking this early, so the wait never ends: bsd_init
+	 * stops inside setconf()/IOFindBSDRoot (run 592, before vfs_mountroot).
+	 * There is nothing to wait for, so do not. */
+	IOLog("nio: skip IOBSD stall in IOFindBSDRoot\n");
 
 	if (mountAttempts++) {
 		IOLog("mount(%d) failed\n", mountAttempts);
